From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:21:30 +0200
Subject: ASoC: rockchip: i2s: Add the I2S_XFER register default

I2S_XFER is the only cached register without a reg_default entry, so
the first cached read of it (the regcache_sync() in runtime resume at
probe) hits a never-initialized flat cache entry and warns:

  rockchip-i2s ff880000.i2s: using zero-initialized flat cache, this
  may cause unexpected behavior

Declare its reset value (0x0, both transfer directions stopped).

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_i2s.c
@@ -630,6 +630,7 @@ static const struct reg_default rockchip_i2s_reg_defaults[] = {
 	{0x08, 0x00071f1f},
 	{0x10, 0x001f0000},
 	{0x14, 0x01f00000},
+	{0x1c, 0x00000000},
 };
 
 static const struct regmap_config rockchip_i2s_regmap_config = {
-- 
